  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe starter tool catalog (`assets/tools/catalog.json`) gets 16 tools:\n\n- `BN-0300`: a 3 mm ball end mill.\n- `BB-0600-R1`: a 6 mm bull nose end mill with a 1 mm corner radius.\n- 14 jobber drills: a tap drill and a clearance drill (ISO 273 medium) for each coarse thread from M3 to M12.\n\n| Thread | Tap drill | Clearance drill |\n|---|---|---|\n| M3 | `DR-0250` | `DR-0340` |\n| M4 | `DR-0330` | `DR-0450` |\n| M5 | `DR-0420` | `DR-0550` |\n| M6 | `DR-0500` | `DR-0660` |\n| M8 | `DR-0680` | `DR-0900` |\n| M10 | `DR-0850` | `DR-1100` |\n| M12 | `DR-1020` | `DR-1350` |\n\nEach new tool goes into its family in diameter order. The other tools keep their order.\n\nThe cutting data follows the rules of the catalog's own rows. Below 6 mm, the drill rpm and feed are interpolated between `DR-0200`, `DR-0300`, `DR-0400` and `DR-0600`. Thus a larger drill never turns faster than a smaller drill. From 6 mm up, the drills use the cutting speed and the feed per revolution of `DR-0600`. `docs/decisions/3036-metric-catalog.md` gives each rule and its source.\n\nThe drill flute length is 3 x D on a 0.5 mm step. A length such as 9.9 mm made `spun::tests::a_parametric_holder_stacks_bit_identically_to_the_cylinder` fail: the spun holder band length was 35.00000000000001 and the cylinder was 35.0. A length on a 0.5 mm step is exact in binary. This PR does not change the spun holder code.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick`: green (`tools suites: lib`, `app suites: mcp`).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-app --tests -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Pinning tests:\n  - `catalog_asset_tests::the_catalog_carries_the_metric_hole_drills_and_small_ball_tools` (sizes, kind, flute length, and the rpm order of all drills).\n  - `catalog_asset_tests::the_shipped_asset_parses_and_every_tool_is_valid` (the new `ORDER`).\n  - `mcp::add_tool_picks_the_metric_hole_drills_and_small_ball_tools_by_name` (`list_tool_catalog` shows each tool, and `add_tool` adds it by name).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No air cut or real cut with the new tools.\n- The tool picker in the GUI was not opened. The picker reads the same catalog list.\n\nChangelog: Tool catalog: a 3 mm ball, a 6 mm bull nose, and the metric tap-drill and clearance drills for M3-M12.\n\nEffort: low\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #3036",
